course: dictionary
lesson: 1348
title: Canadian: from Canada
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Canadian is a word about a place. It means from or about Canada, the big country north of the USA. It can also be a word for a person: a Canadian is someone from Canada. Look at the words around it to see which way it is used.
explain: Canadian is an describing word in phrases like «Canadian flag» and «Canadian dollar», and it tells you which flag or money you mean. To check, swap in «from Canada». A Canadian flag is a flag from Canada, so your meaning works.
explain: Context clues help too. «Tiktaalik was a 375-million-year-old fish... and found it in the Canadian Arctic.» The Canadian Arctic is the cold, northern part of Canada, so the words around Canadian tell you where to look.
fact: Canadian means from or about Canada, the big country north of the USA.
fact: A Canadian is a person from Canada.
fact: Canada is the second-largest country in the world.
fact: Canada has two official languages, English and French, and its capital is Ottawa.
fact: The maple leaf is Canada's symbol, and ice hockey, maple syrup and the Mounties are all linked with Canada.
exercise: «...found it in the Canadian Arctic.» In this sentence, what does Canadian mean? | A type of fish | A kind of rock | Very cold, like ice | *From or about Canada
exercise: What is a Canadian? | A type of maple syrup | A kind of ice hockey stick | *A person from Canada | A person from Australia
exercise: What is the capital city of Canada? | Sydney | Toronto | Paris | *Ottawa
test: Mia wears a «Canadian toque» in the snow. What is a toque? | A Canadian ice hockey team | A boat used on lakes | A type of maple syrup | *A woolly hat
test: Canada has two official languages. Which two are they? | English and Spanish | *English and French | Welsh and Irish | French and German
exam: Which word means a person from Canada? | Maple | *Canadian | Capital | Canada
